From: Andrei <andrei@luta.email>
Subject: [PATCH] MinGW: resolve the engine/device link cycle and Winsock

GNU ld resolves static libraries in the order given and does not go
back, unlike the MSVC linker. The game engine library references
symbols defined in the device library (OSDisplaySetBusyState,
ReloadAllTextures, MOTDSystem) while the device library depends on the
engine, so the final link of generalszh.exe failed with undefined
references. Wrap the two in a rescanned link group for MinGW.

FTP.cpp in WWDownload uses listen/accept from Winsock, but ws2_32 only
appeared on the link line ahead of that library (pulled in by GameSpy),
so add it to the MinGW system library list, which is emitted last.
---
diff --git a/Generals/Code/Main/CMakeLists.txt b/Generals/Code/Main/CMakeLists.txt
index b381fca..cdd20e9 100644
--- a/Generals/Code/Main/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Generals/Code/Main/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -9,13 +9,20 @@ endif()
 
 target_link_libraries(g_generals PRIVATE
     comctl32
-    g_gameenginedevice
     gi_always
     imm32
     vfw32
     winmm
 )
 
+if(MINGW)
+    # GNU ld is order sensitive and the engine and device libraries reference
+    # each other, so let the linker rescan the pair until everything resolves.
+    target_link_libraries(g_generals PRIVATE "$<LINK_GROUP:RESCAN,g_gameenginedevice,g_gameengine>")
+else()
+    target_link_libraries(g_generals PRIVATE g_gameenginedevice)
+endif()
+
 # Let 64-bit Windows give this 32-bit process a 4GB address space instead of 2GB.
 if(MSVC)
     target_link_options(g_generals PRIVATE "/LARGEADDRESSAWARE")
diff --git a/GeneralsMD/Code/Main/CMakeLists.txt b/GeneralsMD/Code/Main/CMakeLists.txt
index 6c51c0b..2935187 100644
--- a/GeneralsMD/Code/Main/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/GeneralsMD/Code/Main/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -12,10 +12,17 @@ target_link_libraries(z_generals PRIVATE
     imm32
     vfw32
     winmm
-    z_gameenginedevice
     zi_always
 )
 
+if(MINGW)
+    # GNU ld is order sensitive and the engine and device libraries reference
+    # each other, so let the linker rescan the pair until everything resolves.
+    target_link_libraries(z_generals PRIVATE "$<LINK_GROUP:RESCAN,z_gameenginedevice,z_gameengine>")
+else()
+    target_link_libraries(z_generals PRIVATE z_gameenginedevice)
+endif()
+
 # Let 64-bit Windows give this 32-bit process a 4GB address space instead of 2GB.
 if(MSVC)
     target_link_options(z_generals PRIVATE "/LARGEADDRESSAWARE")
diff --git a/cmake/mingw.cmake b/cmake/mingw.cmake
index b166fbe..ac78d40 100644
--- a/cmake/mingw.cmake
+++ b/cmake/mingw.cmake
@@ -69,6 +69,7 @@ if(MINGW)
         uuid        # COM GUIDs
         vfw32       # Video for Windows (AVIFile functions)
         winmm       # Multimedia (timeGetTime, etc.)
+        ws2_32      # Winsock (listen/accept in WWDownload FTP.cpp)
     )
 
     # Note: MinGW-w64 does not provide comsuppw (COM support utilities library).
